From e8c51f68a6c3ce854bd5d96431782102d7d4b630 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 18:55:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] netd: don't restart zygote when netd restarts

netd's onrestart hook restarts zygote so the framework rebinds after
mainline netd module updates.  zygote's own onrestart restarts netd, so
on a gsi where netd restarts during boot (legacy bpf-less kernels where
netd's bpf init fails), the two hooks feed each other: netd restarts,
killing zygote; zygote's restart kills netd, which kills zygote again --
an endless restart ping-pong that keeps the boot from ever completing
until the vendor watchdog resets the device.

connectivityservice rebinds to netd via binder death recipients anyway,
so drop the zygote restarts.

verified: applies cleanly under both release-builds and debug-builds
sequences.
---
 server/netd.rc | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/server/netd.rc b/server/netd.rc
index 38f7cd4c..fac1db23 100644
--- a/server/netd.rc
+++ b/server/netd.rc
@@ -28,9 +28,13 @@ service netd /system/bin/netd
     # netd is not updatable, but depends on libs provided by tethering apex.
     # Mark it as updatable so init won't start it until all APEX packages are ready.
     updatable
-    # for obvious reasons 'onrestart' doesn't apply to netd1shot above
-    onrestart restart zygote
-    onrestart restart zygote_secondary
+    # upstream restarts zygote whenever netd restarts so the framework rebinds
+    # after mainline module updates.  on a gsi with legacy bpf-less kernels netd
+    # can restart during boot, and zygote's own onrestart restarts netd -- the
+    # two hooks feed each other and produce an endless zygote/netd restart
+    # ping-pong that prevents boot completion (watchdog eventually resets the
+    # device).  connectivityservice rebinds to netd via binder death
+    # recipients anyway, so the zygote kill is unnecessary here.
 
